flf2a$ 5 5 7 -1 14
blocks, by the sigil authors -- https://github.com/cb1kenobi/sigil

A five-row block font, written for the sigil demos and licensed MIT with the
rest of that repository. Uppercase only: a lowercase letter draws the capital,
because five rows have no room for a descender.

It stops after ASCII 126, which a .flf is allowed to do -- so the seven Deutsch
characters the format lists next are simply not in it, and a renderer asked for
one has to have an answer. That is deliberate: it is half of what the demo shows.

The space character is drawn out of hardblanks rather than out of spaces, so the
word gap survives a kerned or smushed render instead of collapsing into its
neighbours. Full width is what it declares, because every glyph already carries
one blank column of right bearing.
